## Bitcoin Core `sighash.json`

`src/legacy_kat_vectors.zig` reproduces the official legacy (pre-segwit)
`SignatureHash()` reference-oracle corpus published by the Bitcoin Core
project at `src/test/data/sighash.json` (fetched 2026-08 from `master`).
Every row is included except those whose `script` field contains byte `0xab`
(`OP_CODESEPARATOR`, out of scope — see `sighash_legacy.zig`'s module doc
comment): 290 of the 500 rows pass that mechanical, row-content-based filter
and are vendored, unfiltered further. Each row's `raw_transaction` / `script`
/ `input_index` / `hashType` / `signature_hash` is transcribed by script,
never hand-typed.

